{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516727-how-big-is-the-abyss","id":1516727,"title":"How big is the Abyss?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-29T20:45:56-07:00","id":1516727,"title":"How big is the Abyss?","content":"Just how vast is the Abyss, and how large is its numbers of spirit prisoners? I am trying to determine if there is room for the Ancestor Spirit of one of the Lost Breeds to be in there. I assume the Nightmaster or the Black Spiral Dancers would have chucked it in to the maw of the Abyss if they stumbled across it, but the Abyss is ancient and might be the size of Texas, so who knows what is actually down there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T23:32:19-07:00","id":1516737,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is infinite yet traversable. In general the Umbra doesn't work by our conceptions of space and mostly serves as a narrative driven mythic space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T00:15:47-07:00","id":1516739,"title":"","content":"Yeah; all the Umbral realms are infinite, even the ones like CyberRealm wich is basically Spider City (uptown, downtown, the Pit) and the Computer Web above... and Mikaboshi's Wicked City, his Hell in Yomi &quot;invading&quot; it, the Yama King's domain adjoins the CyberRealm in those areas of the Near Realms that overlap the Middle Kingdom.<br /> Yet sill, it is infinite<br /> Pangaea is a reflection of primal Earth, logically it is only &quot;Earth&quot; ocean and one continent, still, infinite <br /> The Abyss or any other realm likewise<br /> <br /> Fun fact: there are actually multiple different sizes of infinity, they're notated by various alephs (nd there are infinite alephs. so aleph 20 is bigger than aleph 4, but aleph 20 is smaller than aleph aleph aleph 44.) so aleph null is how many counting numbers, (1, 2, 3, 4, .... infinity) and aleph one is how many real numbers are in between 0 and 1 (0.0000001, 0.2249043).<br /> Aleph one is actually physically LARGER than aleph null, even though they're both infinite.<br /> (Search up &quot;cantor's diagonalization proof&quot; to find out why)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:19:55-07:00","id":1516783,"title":"","content":"So then should the number of spirits trapped down there be infinite? And I\u2019m guessing an Ancestor Spirit of an Apis or a Grondr is could easily be down there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:26:42-07:00","id":1516784,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> And yes<br /> Tho' you can toss Lord Spider's Web in to the mix<br /> <br /> it was mentioned in the Hengeyokai: Shapeshifters if the East, under the Yin Realms (p 49)<br /> <br /> <b>Yin Realm</b><br /> The Yin Realms are dark places of death and stillness and the hengeyokai, creatures distilled of purest life, are decidedly uncomfortable there. Western shapechangers rarely have the ability to travel to the Yin Realms, which they know as the Dark Umbra.(...)<br /> <br /> <b>Lord Spider's Web</b><br /> Dark and mysterious, Lord Spider's Realm is a quiet place far from the other Realms of the Umbra. It is a titanic web that crosses a gulf so vast that one edge cannot be seen from the other. Unlike the metallic webs commonly associated with the Weaver, this place is more of a natural cobweb, gently fluttering with a cold wind. Lord Spider's Web catches many spirits and objects.<br /> Some believe that Lord Spider is a benevolent spirit,trying to save the lost of the Umbra from the Void. Many hengeyokai have found mummified corpses of Banes and centipedes, even Pattern Spiders, along the web. Some say that Lord Spider was once the lover of the Weaver herself, and now weaves his cobweb in mourning, hoping that he can catch thespirit of his lost love. The Kumo murmur the name of Marawa,and superstitiously avoid this place for fear of offending their great totem. Many hengeyokai say that Lord Spider is long dead; none living have ever seen the spirit.<br /> But sometimes, those who have traveled along this webway feel the web shake and vibrate with incredible force and hear distant screams...<br /> The hengeyokai agree that Lord Spider's Web must span the Abyss, but at what point no one is certain. They know that Lord Spider's Web extends beyond the bounds of the Yin Realm, and the brave have followed the webs to other Realms and secret places.<br /> The Tengu say that the web is not just a single layer, but rather an immense basket, growing thicker and stickier toward the center. They also say that the webs vibrate violently close to the center, as if a titanic struggle were being waged in the center of the web.<br /> <br /> <i>Sample denizen</i><br /> There are no spirits native to Lord Spider's Web, and those that enter the Realm are usually discovered in the form of desiccated husks along the web's strands.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:27:49-07:00","id":1516786,"title":"","content":"Damn this thrice-cursed spam-filter!!!<br /> Okay, so again<br /> Maybe it wont be swallowed by the forum this time...<br /> <br /> Yes<br /> And yes<br /> Tho' you can toss Lord Spider's Web in to the mix<br /> <br /> it was mentioned in the Hengeyokai: Shapeshifters if the East, under the Yin Realms (p 49)<br /> <br /> <b>Yin Realm</b><br /> The Yin Realms are dark places of death and stillness and the hengeyokai, creatures distilled of purest life, are decidedly uncomfortable there. Western shapechangers rarely have the ability to travel to the Yin Realms, which they know as the Dark Umbra.(...)<br /> <br /> <b>Lord Spider's Web</b><br /> Dark and mysterious, Lord Spider's Realm is a quiet place far from the other Realms of the Umbra. It is a titanic web that crosses a gulf so vast that one edge cannot be seen from the other. Unlike the metallic webs commonly associated with the Weaver, this place is more of a natural cobweb, gently fluttering with a cold wind. Lord Spider's Web catches many spirits and objects.<br /> Some believe that Lord Spider is a benevolent spirit,trying to save the lost of the Umbra from the Void. Many hengeyokai have found mummified corpses of Banes and centipedes, even Pattern Spiders, along the web. Some say that Lord Spider was once the lover of the Weaver herself, and now weaves his cobweb in mourning, hoping that he can catch thespirit of his lost love. The Kumo murmur the name of Marawa,and superstitiously avoid this place for fear of offending their great totem. Many hengeyokai say that Lord Spider is long dead; none living have ever seen the spirit.<br /> But sometimes, those who have traveled along this webway feel the web shake and vibrate with incredible force and hear distant screams...<br /> The hengeyokai agree that Lord Spider's Web must span the Abyss, but at what point no one is certain. They know that Lord Spider's Web extends beyond the bounds of the Yin Realm, and the brave have followed the webs to other Realms and secret places.<br /> The Tengu say that the web is not just a single layer, but rather an immense basket, growing thicker and stickier toward the center. They also say that the webs vibrate violently close to the center, as if a titanic struggle were being waged in the center of the web.<br /> <br /> <i>Sample denizen</i><br /> There are no spirits native to Lord Spider's Web, and those that enter the Realm are usually discovered in the form of desiccated husks along the web's strands.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:52:01-07:00","id":1516790,"title":"","content":"N/A Tralala","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 06-30-2023, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T09:15:50-07:00","id":1516799,"title":"","content":"It's hillarious but lord spider's web spans the abyss in my games by default. i forgot it wasnt that necessarilly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T09:20:18-07:00","id":1516800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516727-how-big-is-the-abyss?p=1516739#post1516739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pangaea is a reflection of primal Earth, logically it is only &quot;Earth&quot; ocean and one continent, still, infinite<br /> The Abyss or any other realm likewise\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Pangea is a thing is Werewolf the Apocalypse?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T09:37:41-07:00","id":1516801,"title":"","content":"You can basically find anything and everything that have been lost or that have disappeared in the abyss, the difficulty is to go, find it, get it and come back without turning mad or die.<br /> <br /> Yeah Pangea is one of the mean umbral realms. It embodies the earth as it was 'before', there is no werewolf tribes there, dinosaurs, early 'humans' tribes and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T10:34:44-07:00","id":1516807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516727-how-big-is-the-abyss?p=1516800#post1516800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pangea is a thing is Werewolf the Apocalypse?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> Pangaea is an Umbral realm, the reflection of primal Earth, showing the world as it was before civilization, human history, and even the Impergium. It\u2019s a time when the continents of Earth were as one, a re-creation tempered with anachronism and long-forgotten, atavistic horrors. Dinosaur kings and Mokol\u00e9 shapechangers claim vast territories of Pangaea, and spirits resembling the many stages of human ancestry hunt creatures that humans never knew. Garou staying in this realm for too long disconnect from their former lives and possibly even from their genetic origins. Some begin to degenerate into more primitive species that may or may not have ever existed, gaining freakish abilities that fade when they leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T06:27:30-07:00","id":1516885,"title":"","content":"I imagine the abyss and many realms like it to be infinite from the point of view of it's inhabitants, but simultaneously not very big. On the horizontal plane, places in the abyss might correspond to earth, and like traveling the globe, if you keep traveling west you'll end up where you started. In terms of verticality, There is no bottom, there is no top, ascension and descension are very personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}